#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:1
msgid "Getting and Setting Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:3
msgid "Exporting `just` Variables"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:5
msgid ""
"Assignments prefixed with the `export` keyword will be exported to recipes "
"as environment variables:"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:8
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"export RUST_BACKTRACE := \"1\"\n"
"\n"
"test:\n"
"  # will print a stack trace if it crashes\n"
"  cargo test\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:16
msgid ""
"Parameters prefixed with a `$` will be exported as environment variables:"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:18
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"test $RUST_BACKTRACE=\"1\":\n"
"  # will print a stack trace if it crashes\n"
"  cargo test\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:24
msgid ""
"You can also use the `[env(NAME, VALUE)]` attribute to export environment "
"variables to a specific recipe:"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:27
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"[env(\"RUST_BACKTRACE\", \"1\")]\n"
"test:\n"
"  # will print a stack trace if it crashes\n"
"  cargo test\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:34
msgid ""
"Exported variables and parameters are not exported to backticks in the same "
"scope."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:36
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"export WORLD := \"world\"\n"
"# This backtick will fail with \"WORLD: unbound variable\"\n"
"BAR := `echo hello $WORLD`\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:42
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"# Running `just a foo` will fail with \"A: unbound variable\"\n"
"a $A $B=`echo $A`:\n"
"  echo $A $B\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:48
msgid ""
"When [export](export.html) is set, all `just` variables are exported as "
"environment variables."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:51
msgid "Unexporting Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:53
msgid ""
"Environment variables can be unexported with the `unexport` "
"keyword<sup>1.29.0</sup>:"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:69
msgid "Getting Environment Variables from the Environment"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:71
msgid ""
"Environment variables from the environment are passed automatically to the "
"recipes."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:74
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"print_home_folder:\n"
"  @echo \"HOME is: '${HOME}'\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:84
msgid "Setting `just` Variables from Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-and-setting-environment-variables.md:86
msgid ""
"Environment variables can be propagated to `just` variables using the "
"`env()` function. See [environment-variables](functions.html#environment-"
"variables)."
msgstr ""
